docs: record the transparent-flash investigation

Adds docs/TRANSPARENT_FLASH_INVESTIGATION.md: the full record of chasing
the translucent rectangle that flashes at launch and on the first visit to
the Installed tab.

It is written to stop the next person repeating the dead ends:

- CopyFromScreen cannot capture a WebView2 GPU composition layer, so the
  screenshots this investigation kept 'proving' things with were not showing
  the artefact at all. The only reliable observer for a sub-second flash is
  the user's own eyes, which is why the search ended up bisecting by
  commenting startup tasks out.
- Launch flash: root cause was `dotnet --list-runtimes` in
  is_dotnet_installed(). Creating a process on Windows briefly stalls every
  thread in the parent, and spawn_blocking does not help because the stall is
  in process creation itself. Fixed by probing the filesystem instead.
- First Installed visit: the scan in we_list_installed holds the
  RwLock<WallpaperEngineClient> read lock for its whole duration, and every
  synchronous we_* command runs on the main thread and blocks on that lock.
  Not fixed yet; the document spells out the correct shape and warns about
  the temporary-value lifetime trap that made one attempt worse.

Also records the current bisect state of useBootstrap.ts (five startup tasks
commented out) so whoever resumes knows it is mid-experiment, not final.